# Domain model — hard rules

## Hierarchy
- Tasks are ALWAYS nested under a milestone. No exceptions.
- Milestones and tasks are NEVER at the same tree level.
- Tasks with no milestone → virtual "no milestone" node. They must stay visible.

## Sync sets
Two named sets, fixed for MVP:
- `Podstawowe słowniki` — dictionaries (spaces, folders, lists), slow cadence
- `Zadania` — tasks, fast incremental cadence

Each set carries independent state:
```
lastSuccessAt: Timestamp | null
lastFailureAt: Timestamp | null
errorDescription: string | null
```
A new failure does NOT overwrite `lastSuccessAt`. Both timestamps coexist.

## Write-back safety
Local changes stage in a **pending queue**. They reach ClickUp only after the
user explicitly approves them. Never push automatically, never push silently.

## Token security
The ClickUp personal API token is the only secret. Never log it, never embed it
in source, never include it in error messages shown to the user.
